 "text": "I found 30 defects in the spec and submitted them through the review tool. The most serious are below.\n\n**Critical**\n- **Sales report (REQ-85 vs REQ-86):** the two requirements define the same report differently. One counts delivered orders by delivery date, the other counts all non-cancelled orders by order date, so the totals disagree.\n\n**High**\n- **Office Staff company editing (REQ-81):** it lets Office Staff create and edit companies, including price-list assignment and active status. REQ-80 and REQ-28 make those admin-only.\n- **Card payments (spec assumptions):** the spec overrides the human's accepted ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) and lists online payments as out of scope. That reverses a decision the human made.\n- **Dashboard field (REQ-67 vs REQ-68):** the same `failedImports` field is defined two ways: since the last successful import, or in the last 7 days.\n- **Missing permission paths:**\n  - REQ-9/REQ-10 don't say what a password reset does for deactivated users, pending invitees or users of inactive companies. A reset could get round deactivation or invitation acceptance.\n  - Order emails (REQ-47) keep going to a Buyer after they are deactivated or moved to another company (AC-16.4), which leaks the old company's data.\n  - Nothing stops an administrator deactivating or demoting themselves, or the last administrator.\n- **Duplicate performance targets:** NFR-1/NFR-2, NFR-3/NFR-4 and NFR-5/6/7 each give different numbers for the same thing.\n\n**Medium**\n- **Account enumeration (REQ-3 vs REQ-2):** locking and inactive-account messages (423 and 403) only happen for real accounts. Unknown emails always get 401, which defeats REQ-2's identical-error rule.\n- **Missing import file (REQ-31 vs REQ-33):** one says no new file means no change; the other logs a failure. Processed files are moved away, so every quiet night may log a failure.\n- **Role and invitation rules:** REQ-12 and REQ-17 limit roles to Buyer and Office Staff, but REQ-13 and REQ-18 allow Administrator.\n- **Session timeout (NFR-15 vs NFR-16):** 30 minutes vs 60 minutes, and the values are fixed in code.\n- **Missing error paths:**\n  - Submitting an empty basket.\n  - Staff removing the last line of an order.\n  - Inviting an email address that already has an account.\n  - Switching a user to Buyer without a company.\n  - Retiring a category that still has products.\n  - Removing a company's only or in-use delivery address.\n- **Weak tests:** AC-4.5 and AC-45.2 accept \"401 or 403\". Several tests check internal database rows or call internal calculators rather than a public endpoint.\n\n**Low:** a fixed 7-day dashboard window, an unnamed currency with no setting for it, and a stock CSV column mapping that is fixed in code.\n\nThe full list with severities is in the submission.",
